0000:                   ********************************************************************
0000:                   * PipeMan - OS-9 Pipe File Manager
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Some tests under NitrOS-9:
0000:                   *
0000:                   * 'show grf.3.a | eat'  (eat is cat, but just does a I$ReadLn, and not I$WritLn)
0000:                   * April 10, 1996  14:05:15
0000:                   * April 10, 1996  14:07:47
0000:                   *          15.2 seconds per iteration
0000:                   *          i.e. everything but the screen writes
0000:                   * 
0000:                   * fast SCF+fast pipe
0000:                   * 'show grf.3.a | cat', 10 times
0000:                   * April 10, 1996  13:17:54
0000:                   * April 10, 1996  13:21:57
0000:                   *          24.3 seconds per iteration
0000:                   *          9.1 solely for pipes
0000:                   * 
0000:                   * fast SCF+old slow pipe
0000:                   * April 10, 1996  13:30:24
0000:                   * April 10, 1996  13:38:04
0000:                   *          46.0 seconds per iteration
0000:                   *          30.8 solely for pipes
0000:                   * 
0000:                   *          speedup percent is (30.8-9.1)/30.8 = 70%
0000:                   * 
0000:                   *          Pipes are more than doubled in speed!
0000:                   *
0000:                   * 32 byte read and write buffers
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *   4      ????/??/??  Alan DeKok
0000:                   * Enhanced and re-written.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   5r0    2003/08/27  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Back-ported from OS-9 Level Two to OS-9 Level One.
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   PipeMan
0000:                            ttl   OS-9 Pipe File Manager
0000:                   
0000:                            ifp1
0000:                            use   defsfile
0000:                            use   pipe.d
0000:                            use   scf.d
0000:                            endc
0000:                   
